4) Secure VNets, subnets, NSGs, and service endpoints for ML pipelines

Security principles: minimize public endpoints; use Private Link & Private Endpoints; least privilege; defense-in-depth.
VNet & subnet design
Create separate subnets per function: bastion, infra, aks, storage, sql.
Use network segmentation to limit blast radius.
Use UDR (User Defined Routes) only where needed, e.g., route outbound to Azure Firewall.
NSGs (Network Security Groups)
Apply NSGs to subnets (prefer subnet-level for simplicity).
Default deny inbound; open explicit ports:
AKS node pool: allow node kubelet/agent flows from/control plane.
Only allow SSH/RDP from jump/bastion IPs (or use Azure Bastion).
Example rules:
Deny 0.0.0.0/0 inbound except necessary egress to required endpoints.
Allow management IPs (DevOps) to bastion subnet.
Private Endpoints & Service Endpoints
Prefer Private Endpoints (Private Link) for Storage Accounts, Key Vault, ACR, Azure SQL. This gives a NIC in your VNet and no public network path.
Service Endpoints are older; they simplify routing to PaaS from VNet but still use public addresses (less preferred).
Configure DNS so the PaaS resource resolves to private IP (Azure Private DNS Zones).
Azure Firewall / NVA
Put Azure Firewall as outbound egress point, with FQDN filtering to allow only required external services (e.g., container registry, apt repositories).
Consider forced tunneling to on-prem for compliance.
Identity & Secrets
Use Managed Identities for AKS components, Data Factory, Azure ML; avoid embedding credentials.
Keep secrets in Azure Key Vault with RBAC and Private Endpoint. Access via Managed Identity.
Use Key Vault references for App Service and used provider-managed integrations.
RBAC, Policies, & Monitoring
Enforce Azure AD RBAC for resource access.
Use Azure Policy to restrict public IP creation, allowed regions, and SKU blacklists.
Log NSG flow logs to Log Analytics for monitoring.
Example: Secure AKS networking
AKS with Azure CNI or Azure CNI overlay for IP allocation into VNet (helps with Private endpoints).
Place AKS ingress behind NGINX Ingress with WAF or use Application Gateway + AGIC with Private IP.
Ensure ACR access via Private Endpoint or use ACR tokens and Private Link.

